From 7d29e1f31515c76202ec4c5bc4e5d52157e36c04 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: khunmax2 <khuncharoenmax1@hotmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 02:47:43 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(openmaic): serve the course studio under a path, not a
 port
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The deployment host will not open a second port — policy, not configuration —
so the embed's port-of-its-own shape left the studio unreachable. The remaining
route is a path on the 443 that is already open.

basePath is not enough on its own. It prefixes <Link>, the router and /_next/
assets; it does not touch a URL the app writes itself, and this app writes 74
fetch('/api/...') calls across 44 files plus three EventSource streams. Under a
prefix every one of them leaves for the root of the host.

A reverse proxy would normally absorb that, but this host already serves
/sansarnnews, /research-helper, /dol, /deepwitya, /opdc-assistant and
/deepwitya2 — /api at its root belongs to other people's applications, and a
rule there would sit in front of all of them. So the app prefixes its own URLs.
Rewriting 44 files would be 44 files to re-apply on every subtree pull;
rewriting the two globals they funnel through is one, and it is inert when
NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_PATH is unset, so the port shape and upstream are untouched.

EventSource matters as much as fetch: the workbench streams over SSE, and
wrapping only fetch would have left it silently dead. For /public, three choke
points cover the 43 files that reference one — AvatarImage, DEFAULT_BRAND, and
a pass over PROVIDERS beside the applyModelMetadata call already there.

The failure this prevents is not a network error. It is the studio showing an
access-code login box nobody configured, because /api/access-code/status fails
and the guard treats an error as locked.

Verified against a real build: the value is inlined into the CLIENT bundle
(let t="/course-studio-app"), which is what would have made the wrapper a silent
no-op otherwise. Under the prefix the page, /api, /brand-wordmark.png, /avatars
and /logos all answer 200 and the page is byte-identical to the prerendered
home page; at the root all of them 404. Eight unit tests cover the rewrite
rules. The gatekeeper needed no change — it is path-transparent, and its one
literal path is only reached directly on loopback.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
